<BaseLayout title="About & How We Test" description="How FullTVBox tests streaming devices, scores them, and stays independent — our methodology, rating scale, and editorial policy.">
  <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 py-14">
    <span class="label text-signal">// Channel 06 — Station ID</span>
    <h1 class="font-display font-900 text-4xl sm:text-5xl tracking-tight mt-1 mb-8">About &amp; How We Test</h1>

    <div class="smpte-bars h-1 w-full mb-10 opacity-60"></div>

    <div class="prose prose-invert prose-lg max-w-none prose-bench
      prose-headings:font-display prose-headings:text-ink
      prose-p:text-ink/85 prose-li:text-ink/85">

      <p>
        FullTVBox is an independent review site dedicated to helping you find the right streaming
        device. We test Android TV boxes, streaming sticks, and media players — and we tell you
        what we actually think, without manufacturer influence.
      </p>

      <h2>Independence &amp; Funding</h2>
      <p>
        We buy or borrow every device we review. No freebies accepted from manufacturers, no paid
        placements, and no sponsored rankings — a brand cannot pay to score higher or appear on our
        <a href="/best-picks">best-picks</a> list. Our only revenue comes from affiliate
        commissions: if you click a product link and buy, we earn a small percentage at no extra
        cost to you. Those links never change our verdict, and we routinely recommend cheaper
        devices over more expensive ones. How we handle your data is covered on our
        <a href="/privacy">privacy page</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>How We Test</h2>
      <p>
        Every device goes through at least two weeks of daily, real-world use on a 4K HDR TV — not
        a spec-sheet skim. We evaluate each one against the same criteria so reviews are directly
        comparable:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Setup &amp; first boot</strong> — how quickly and painlessly it gets running, account requirements, and bloat.</li>
        <li><strong>Speed &amp; responsiveness</strong> — boot time, app launch times, and how it holds up when multitasking.</li>
        <li><strong>Picture &amp; sound</strong> — 4K HDR playback, Dolby Vision/HDR10+ support, and audio passthrough (Dolby Atmos, DTS).</li>
        <li><strong>Streaming reliability</strong> — buffering and stability over both Wi-Fi and wired Ethernet where available.</li>
        <li><strong>Interface &amp; ads</strong> — how clean or cluttered the home screen is and how aggressively it pushes promoted content.</li>
        <li><strong>Remote &amp; voice</strong> — ergonomics, TV controls, and voice/assistant accuracy.</li>
        <li><strong>App &amp; ecosystem support</strong> — availability of major apps, sideloading, and platform lock-in.</li>
        <li><strong>Long-term software support</strong> — update history and how well older models age.</li>
        <li><strong>Value</strong> — what you get for the price versus the alternatives.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Our Rating Scale</h2>
      <p>
        Scores run from 1.0 to 5.0 and reflect a device relative to its price and category — a
        great $50 stick and a great $200 box can both earn a high score for being the best at what
        they do.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>4.5–5.0</strong> — class-leading; buy with confidence.</li>
        <li><strong>4.0–4.4</strong> — very good, with minor trade-offs.</li>
        <li><strong>3.5–3.9</strong> — solid but compromised; right only for specific buyers.</li>
        <li><strong>Below 3.5</strong> — notable flaws; proceed with caution.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We revisit reviews as software changes and prices move, and mark them with an
        <strong>updated</strong> date when we do — so a score always reflects the device as it is
        today, not at launch.
      </p>

      <h2>Who We Are</h2>
      <p>
        Reviews and guides are produced by the <strong>FullTVBox Test Bench</strong> — our in-house
        team of home theater enthusiasts who got tired of review sites that just reprint spec
        sheets. We write the reviews we wished existed before buying our own devices, and every
        article carries the Test Bench byline.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Found an error or have a device you'd like us to review? Reach us at{' '}
        <a href="mailto:hello@fulltvbox.com">hello@fulltvbox.com</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
